# Site assembly

During the first build of the marketing site the user says when to commit and when to open a PR.

- One pull request is one page
- One commit is one new block on that page
- Leave the work uncommitted until asked
- Branch off `main`. Do not start the next page inside the current page's branch

## Homepage

Art direction is the third homepage mock: open Enso, serif wordmark, paper background, vermilion call to action, dark closing band. Sections differ on purpose. Do not introduce a section registry or a generic block renderer.

`app/page.tsx` renders `HomeSections`. That component only stacks section components, in this order:

1. `hero`
2. `manifesto`
3. `projects`
4. `solutions`
5. `capabilities`
6. `design`
7. `process`

The closing band is the site footer: lead, form, contacts, and copyright. It is not a homepage section. The header action points at `/#contact` on that footer.

Each block owns:

- `components/home/<section>/<section>.tsx`
- `content/home/<section>.ts` with `ru` and `en` of the same type

`HomeSections` passes `locale` into every section. Wrap the stack in `LocalePanels` when the first section needs copy.

Shared chrome lives in `components/site/` (header, nav, footer, logo). Its copy stays in `content/messages/`. Nav targets are `/#studio`, `/#projects`, `/#solutions`, `/#capabilities`, `/#process`. The header action points at `/#contact`.

A task touches one section. Do not restyle the others in the same change. A section is done when both locales render and the desktop composition follows the mock.
